==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|xgender}} {{q|abbreviation}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|en|trans|gender}}. First used in English by John Oliven in 1965,<ref name="Bevan"/> the term had acquired its current senses by the 1990s (by which time it had also largely displaced the earlier term {{m|en|transsexual}}; see usage notes).<ref name="TR2006"/>

